   <standOff><listPerson><person xml:id="person3747"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">maitreya</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'phags pa byams pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byams pa mgon po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">maitreyanātha</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P6118</idno><idno type="APIS">3747</idno><note type="comment">Future Buddha held as the author of the works that come to be designated as the "Five Jewels of Maitreya" (ID:6167).</note></person><person xml:id="person3756"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">asaṅga</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon thogs med</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">thogs myed</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P6117</idno><idno type="APIS">3756</idno></person><person xml:id="person6025"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos gshes</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཆོས་གཤེས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos she</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">6025</idno></person><person xml:id="person8399"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mkhan po zul phu ba</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">མཁན་པོ་ཟུལ་ཕུ་བ</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">8399</idno></person></listPerson><listBibl><bibl xml:id="work3749"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ratnagotravibhāga</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rātnagotravibhāga mahāyānottaratantraśāstra</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">uttaratantra</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">theg pa chen po rgyud bla ma'i bstan bcos</title><author ref="person:3747">maitreya</author><author ref="person:3756">asaṅga</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">The authorship of the work comes to be ascribed to the future Buddha Maitreya (ID:3747) in the Indian tradition from the 11th c. onward and in the Tibetan tradition. On earlier witnesses ascribing the authorship to Sāramati or Sthiramati, see [BAQ9MH4T]: 20-27. No attribution of that work to Asaṅga (ID:3756) was located in Indian sources, but the colophon of the Tibetan translation by rNgog Blo ldan shes rab ascribes the verses to Maitreya and the prose commentary to Asaṅga ([BAQ9MH4T]: 27-28).&#13;
There are six Tibetan translations, only that by rNgog Blo ldan shes rab and Sajjana is currently extant ([BAQ9MH4T]: chap. 6).</note><idno type="APIS">3749</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work5219"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bstan bcos rgyud bla ma'i gsal byed bsam mi khyab kyi yi ge</title><title xml:lang="bo">བསྟན་བཅོས་རྒྱུད་བླ་མའི་གསལ་བྱེད་བསམ་མི་ཁྱབ་ཀྱི་ཡི་གེ</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bsam gyis mi khyab gdam ngag</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bstan bcos rgyud bla ma'i gdam ngag bsam mi khyab kyi yi ge</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><author ref="person:6025">chos gshes</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">Topical outline of the Ratnagotravibhāga (ID:3749); lemmata for each delineated section are provided in interlinear notes in (ID:5218).&#13;
&#13;
At the end of the text, one finds a history of the transmission of the teachings of the Ratnagotravibhāga (ID:3749) along with the Dharmadharmatāvibhaṅga (ID:5634) which is nearly identical to the one in sKyo ston (ID:4052)'s Theg chen rgyud bla ma'i gdams pa (ID:4838).&#13;
The lineage itself diverges after Bla ma do pa (ID:5613).&#13;
&#13;
Author according to [8H6M69W4], No. 15776: bla ma spu rangs pa. This figure is mentioned in the succession of masters in the "lo rgyus" section of the text, but the lineage ends with dge slong chos she.</note><relatedItem type="commentaryOn" target="work:3749"/><idno type="APIS">5219</idno></bibl></listBibl><listRelation><relation xml:id="rel1000" name="author-of" active="#person6025" passive="#work5219" type="positive"/><relation xml:id="rel7639" name="lineage-predecessor-of" active="#person8399" passive="#person6025" type="positive"/></listRelation></standOff><text>
